From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: timvdhoorn <timvdhoorn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:29:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] feat(server): push agent activity directly to APNs

A server with an APNs auth key in its secret store (direct-push-apns) sends
agent notifications and Live Activity updates to APNs itself, for an app
built under its own bundle id that the T3 relay cannot reach. Devices register
their push and Live Activity tokens over the environment connection
(server.registerPushDevice, server.registerPushLiveActivity) and read the
current card with server.getPushActivitySnapshot.

The delivery rules are ported from the relay. The existing activity publisher
feeds the direct sink, so deduplication, confirmation and the startup filter
stay shared. Each server pushes only its own threads and only ends a Live
Activity it filled itself. Without a key the server behaves as upstream.
